  "body": "Found by the #926 per-post script suites (recorded stream `rotary`, posted on `assets/machines/tilthead.mch`, a head with rotaries A and B only).\n\n**What is wrong.** `fanuc.cps` `tilt()` writes all three angle words on the first tilted block - `G00 X0 Y0 Z20 A30 B0 C0` - although the machine states no C rotary. `missingLetter` only checks letters that turn (non-zero), so a C0 word for a machine without C passes. A control without a C axis alarms on the address (or, on a machine where C is some other function, commands it).\n\nWhy P2: wrong output, but the control refuses it; no gouge.\n\nDone means: the tilt words name only rotaries the machine states (a stated-zero letter of an absent rotary is not written), pinned by the #926 `rotary` golden of `fanuc` (listed as a known bug in `crates/post/tests/recorded/mod.rs`).\n",
